I just chmod ed the whole dir a+rwx and that didn't help
How are you restarting Tomcat?
root#&gt; /etc/init.d/tomcat-5.5 restart
Also, find out where the Tomcat work directory is, and: shut down Tomcat, rm -rf CATALINA_HOME/work/*, then restart Tomcat.
I'm pretty sure that your init script for Tomcat on gentoo is not reliable.  That is: when you tell it to stop Tomcat, you cannot rely on the Tomcat JVM process being shut down when the script says it's done.
So, that means you have to use ps and find out for yourself.. which means you can't use the restart feature because the init script will start Tomcat again before the first one is down.
So, you should stop tomcat, ps ax | grep java and make sure it's really gone, then start Tomcat.. and you should do those exact steps each time you restart it or else you can't be sure you restarted it.
