CONVERSATION:
any ideas how to redirect any connections from 8080 to 80 port ?
iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -p tcp -d ip --dport 8080 -j DNAT --to-destination ip:22 don't work
hello everyone
I'm migrating to a new server and I'm using iptables to make the transition as smooth as possible - to bridge the time it takes for all DNS servers to update.
scpecifically I'm telling the old server to redirect all traffic to the new server.
so, to move the e-mail service I'd do:
iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -s 0.0.0.0/0 -d  IP1  -p tcp --dport 25 -j DNAT --to IP2
iptables -t nat -A POSTROUTING -s 0.0.0.0/0 -d IP2  -p tcp --dport 25  -j SNAT --to IP1
this works fine for smtp and imap but this trick doesn't seem to work for ftp.
any ideas? (I get errors on the new server like: &quot;refused PORT some-ip-address,32788 from my-old-server&quot;)
Iskorptixas:  be more specific. you want connections arriving at one IP at port 8080 to be redirected to another IP port 80 correct?
(sorry I can't reply with provate message... freenode is blocking from unregistered users)
does anyone have a suggestion as to where the above &quot;refused PORT&quot; errors might come from?
I want connections arriving at one IP and at port 8080 to be redirected to the same ip port 80
just becouse my isp blocking 1-1024 ports
