and you set map[0] = true;
and then fetch map[0]
if you see what i mean
sorry, i'm not expressing myself well
sorry i didn't understand :)
a3f19f90edf0a0893c7847d08016abe3: the concern comes from the Storage object, where you can get the keys by index, and then index into the keys to get the values
a3f19f90edf0a0893c7847d08016abe3: there is a clash if someone sets the key &quot;0&quot; and then fetches the property &quot;0&quot; -- it'll return &quot;0&quot; because that's the name of the key
but then if you fetch the property &quot;0&quot;, you'll still just get &quot;0&quot;, not the value of the key &quot;0&quot;
because the keys and the indexes are in the same namespace
i'm wondering whether to ban numeric keys to get around this
or to just say &quot;tough&quot;
69b0d3dfe919a6b860a9fac82de52a7e, i see what you mean now
