CONVERSATION:
whats up
hi
i need advice
ok whats up
ok i have this friend, we&apos;ve been best friends for like 6 years, but weve had issues lately, and he says &apos;he doesnt feel comfortable talk..." | raw="
CONVERSATION:
whats up
hi
i need advice
ok whats up
ok i have this friend, we&apos;ve been best friends for like 6 years, but weve had issues lately, and he says &apos;he doesnt feel comfortable talking to me becuase i&apos;m such an angry person&apos;, and i&apos;m having a hard time not being angry or missing him
like i fluctuate between  being happy that we&apos;re not talking any more because it&apos;s probably for the best, and missing him, and i just wish i could forget he ever existed
i know how you feel. i just got over something like this. do you like him as more than a friend?
nope, totally platonic
what happened was we went to college, and neither of us made a ton of friends right away, so we had dinner together every night, until he made a friend, and then he was like &apos;i&apos;m gonna eat with this guy a couple of nights a week&apos;, but that turned into every single night and he totally ditched me for this other person
which left me eating by myself
well how do u act towards him? do u act angry and call him names and stuff
oh no i don&apos;t call him names or anything, it&apos;s just that alot of times when he would talk ot me, it would be right after i ate dinner by myself and he SAW me eating by myself and didn&apos;t say anything
so i&apos;d be in a bad mood
yeah i dont blame you. well did u explain to him that you feel left out??
yeah believe me i told him
and he doesnt care? doesnt sound like much of a friend
truth
but i&apos;m having a hard time getting over it
like i want to be his friend but i dont, at the same time
i think u should just forget him cause hes obvioulsy forgotten you and make some new friends
yeah easier said than done lol
trust me i know. i jsut got done going thru this. i think u should 1) delete his number 2) dont talk to him via facebook/email 3) make some new friends. do u go to a small school?
no, its a big public school
and i already took care of all the other stuff, phone and email and everything
are u a girl?
yeah
why dont u rush? u make lots of friends there!
i&apos;m a bit hesitant about that, i don&apos;t drink
i don&apos;t really party at all
so? there are lots of girls in sororities that dont drink.. drinnking doesnt = partying. im in a sorority and i only go out sometimes
also i&apos;m not exactly the type you&apos;d look at me and say &apos;sorority girl&apos; if you know what i mean
well... its worth a shot. even if you dont make a sorority you&apos;re gonna meet people that are rushing too. its a great experience
that makes sense
i really appreciate the advice, i can&apos;t really talk to anyone i know about this because they&apos;re all sick of me talking about it because it&apos;s been going on for awhile
and for all you know, you COULD make one! then you&apos;d have so many new friends. where do you go to school&gt;
uconn
there are lots of sororities there! i know how you feel trust me on this one. i had a best friend of like 8 years. plus he was ex boyfriend and now we barely talk because he got into weed
yeah it sucks too cause my best friend, all three of us used to be best friends
and now she&apos;s friends with me and him, but the two of us aren&apos;t friends
so it&apos;s awkward
heres what i think...
i think he needs some time away from you. being best friends with someone THAT long takes a toll on a person. he needs to get out and experience college life.. you should do the same. get out and meet people. rush, go to parties ( u dont have to drink....i cant tell u how many times i bring a bottle of water in my purse, grab a beer bottle, go to the bathroom &amp; pour the beer out and replace it with the water) dont waste your college life worrying about this. if you guys are meant to friends then it&apos;ll happen. boys are weird like this. they need their space. he&apos;s experiincing 100% freedom for the first time. dont worry about him or missing him. the more u think about it, the harder it is
you seriously give great advice
thanks a ton
no problem. i know how ya feel :(
yeah its a crap situation
it is. BUT it makes u stronger. besides guess what-- did u know, explicit: meet, explicit: hot, secrecy: dont tell.""")
