CONVERSATION:
how can i check what username a share has been mapped with a connected windows client
net status shares only shows the IP address of the connection, not user name
are you trying to scri..." | raw="
CONVERSATION:
how can i check what username a share has been mapped with a connected windows client
net status shares only shows the IP address of the connection, not user name
are you trying to script this, or just looking it up when needed?
just when i need to
bloody windows clients with saved password in explorer it seems even when mapping a drive with a dif user, it must try the saved user/pass as well
as long as you don't mind manually typing in, try using the IP address gleaned from net status shares, and grep for it in the output of smbstatus
eg: smbstatus | grep ip.add.re.ss
but i want to find out the username of the connection, not the ip
the username is on the same line as the IP
should be the first thing on the line
i get these columns Service      pid     machine       Connected at
sorry, the second thing on the line
so whats the PID in this case?
hmm process id of the service
i don't get a user column from smbstatus or net status shares
nope, the process id of the smbd daemon handling that service
in this case, user=service
what do you mean... i stll can't find out the username
what version of samba?
3.03 i think. its in share mode
now I see your problem
ok
i'm using samba-3.0.10-1.fc3
ok so what should i do br0
why are you using share mode?
because i failed to set up anonymous printing in user mode. windows clients kept getting access denied.
are you using samba for printing only, or file shares as well?
yep both on this server
1 to be public, 1 to require auth, 1 print share anon
i couldn't work out how to do auth in share mode
share mode is a bit weird
i get 18166: tree connect failed: ERRSRV - ERRbadpw (Bad password - name/password pair in a Tree Connect or Session Setup are invalid.)
are you using any central authentication (active directory, NT)
yeah i don't understand share mode very well
nah, i just want to use shell accounts mapped by smbusers flaccid = flaccid
so for each windows user, you have a posix account on the unix box, correct?
no. i just want guest access for the windows clients
guest for everything except 1 share
then you should probably be using security = user in the global config, and guest allow = yes for each share that doesn't require authentication
i think doing that iirc still returns access denied for the windows clients with the print share
do you mean guest ok = yes?
yes
sorry, was running from memory
when i do that testparm -v with [printers] doesn't show the guest ok = yes param
it's been a while since I used anything other than ads or server for security in samba, so I'll need a couple minutes to double check the settings
thanks heaps npz
hmm that of worked
what worked?
that solution
im just checking
heh the windows client is freezing up
can't even get to print dialog
that's not good
i just don't get it. samba is easy to set up. but despite following examples and manual, things like this happen a lot
lets look at it from a different perspective.  how many client machines do you have?
about 3 windows clients and a few linux
so a fairly small network then.
yep
heh despite the freezing up i got a print job from 1 machine to work
come through as flaccid and not guest however
with the new config?
yeah
i believe that would prolly be it trying the saved password. i wish i knew how to delete saved passwords in windows explorer
it will come through as your username, but it should also allow guest access as well
as far as I know, you can't delete saved passwords, unless you cheat, change the password on the server and let windows ask for a new one
yeah... getting windows to use guest is hard
grr windows
getting windows to behave itself isn't much easier
true
when i print with this config from linux client, it goes in the local queue and doesnt move
are you using cups for printing?
yeah
oh the printer was stopped for some reason
out of paper?
looks like it went through
this is on my notebook cups
another windows client gets this A StartDocPrinter call was not issued
very strange
<a href="http://support.microsoft.com/?kbid=121074">http://support.microsoft.com/?kbid=121074</a>

